### Key Findings & Defect Categorization

1. **Missing Keys in Codebase (Leftover English / Raw Keys - Severity: High):**
   - **Static scan ([`missing_keys_scan.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S5/missing_keys_scan.json)):** **271 distinct keys** invoked via `t(...)` in source files do not exist in [`src/locales/en.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/locales/en.json) (e.g. `NEXT PRAYER`, `Salah Today`, `TRACKERS & CALCULATORS`, `UTILITIES & LOCATION`, `Noble names & attributes`, `Recitations, audio translations...`, `Structured schedules...`).
   - **Runtime impact:** In all non-English locales (`ur`, `ar`, `hi`, `ml`, `si`), `i18next` falls back to returning the key itself, producing noticeable English leakage across 26-34 routes.

2. **Interpolation Token Integrity (Rule 14 Violation - Severity: Medium):**
   - In [`src/locales/ar.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/locales/ar.json), keys `Hizb {n} selected` and `Juz {n} selected` translate the parameter token to `{ن}` instead of retaining exact token `{n}`. While patched at runtime via a custom regex in [`src/lib/i18n.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/lib/i18n.ts#L195-L198), it violates Standing Rule 14.

3. **Hardcoded English Literals in Sheets/Dialogs (Severity: Medium):**
   - [`WomenConsentModal.tsx`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/components/WomenConsentModal.tsx): 10 hardcoded English paragraphs and heading literals bypassing `t(...)` entirely (e.g. *"Your cycle, purity, and worship data are deeply personal..."*, *"Stays on this device"*).
   - [`AdhanReciterModal.tsx`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/components/AdhanReciterModal.tsx): Hardcoded English subtitle (*"Preview adhans with the play button..."*).
   - [`AudioPlayerModal.tsx`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/components/AudioPlayerModal.tsx): Hardcoded empty-state description (*"Choose any surah or reciter from the Quran tab..."*).

4. **RTL Directional Styling / Physical Margins (Severity: Medium):**
   - **Static scan ([`rtl_directional_scan.json`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/reports/audit/evidence/S5/rtl_directional_scan.json)):** **44 files** utilize physical CSS properties (`paddingLeft`, `paddingRight`, `marginLeft`, `marginRight`) rather than logical properties (`paddingStart`, `paddingEnd`, `marginStart`, `marginEnd`). In RTL mode (`ur`, `ar`), these asymmetric offsets do not mirror.

5. **Script Fonts & Numeral Formatting (Severity: Low):**
   - [`src/lib/fonts.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/apps/islamic_app/src/lib/fonts.ts) only bundles Arabic and Latin fonts. Hindi (`hi`), Malayalam (`ml`), and Sinhala (`si`) rely completely on unbundled system font fallbacks. Urdu lacks a dedicated Nastaliq font (falls back to Noto Naskh Arabic).
   - UI numbers (prayer countdowns, hijri dates, tasbih counters, zakat calculator) hardcode Latin digits (0-9) rather than utilizing localized numerals.

